# clang-format must never touch configure_file() templates: reflow inserts
# spaces inside @VAR@ placeholder tokens (e.g. `@NROS_ENTRY_PKG_SYM @`), which
# breaks substitution and generates un-compilable TUs (issue 0159 fallout,
# 701ae4b6a corrupted zephyr_entry_main_c_typed.cpp.in this way).
cmake/templates/*

# PX4 modules follow PX4 style (tab indent, 120 cols, Tools/astyle), not ours.
# Nothing formats these today — both fmt recipes enumerate paths by hand and no
# PX4 tree is among them. This is a GUARD: the day a glob widens to
# `examples/**/*.cpp`, clang-format itself honours this file, so the trees stay
# PX4-shaped rather than being silently reflowed to 4-space. See phase-325 W0.1.
packages/testing/nros-px4-register-check/*
examples/px4/*
